@page "/about"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inherits ApiPageBase

<PageTitle>About PenniesCount</PageTitle>
<h1>About PenniesCount</h1>
<h2>Budget calculations</h2>
<p>Total savings is the sum of current account balances. Headline Total allocated is the amount still available to spend on non-removed items.
    Unallocated is total savings minus this available allocation: positive means spare funds; negative means over-allocation.</p>
<p>Category Funded allocation is total funding to date, including money already drawn down.
    Available to spend is funded allocation minus drawdowns. Funding remaining is target minus funded allocation.
    Required monthly contribution is the recommendation for the next payment, not the whole funding remainder.</p>
<p>Drawdowns do not update accounts: apparent spare funds may be temporary until you manually submit the new account balances.
    Drawdowns do not create another funding requirement. Removed items are excluded from all budget and forecast totals.</p>
<h2>Allocation dates and bank holidays</h2>
<p>Allocations are scheduled for the first working day of each month, skipping weekends and known England-and-Wales bank holidays.
    Without holiday coverage, the estimate uses the first weekday of the month and may change when data becomes available.
    Today's date is excluded only for items with an effective allocation payment recorded today; reversed payments do not count.</p>
<p>Active items spread their funding remainder over remaining allocation dates through the inclusive save-by deadline.
    Items not yet started contribute zero to today's monthly recommendation. Fully funded items need no further contribution.
    With no allocation dates remaining, the full funding remainder is Needed now, including underfunded historic goals.
    Recommendations round upward to the nearest penny; the headline monthly total sums these recommendations.</p>
<h2>Categories</h2>
<p>Purpose categories are chosen when adding an item or editing its details. Existing items remain Uncategorised until edited.</p>
<ul>
    @foreach (var category in Enum.GetValues<SavingsCategory>())
    {
        <li>@Display.PurposeCategoryName(category)</li>
    }
</ul>
<p>Edit details changes only the name, save-by date and purpose category, not funding or ledger history.
    Save by must be on or after the original start date; past dates are allowed. Removed items remain read-only.</p>
<p>Savings terms use the API's local budget date and the save-by deadline: Short term is less than one calendar year away,
    Medium term is one through five years away, Long term is more than five years away, and Historic means a deadline before today.</p>
<h2>Future look</h2>
<p>The charts project the current month and the following 23 months. Each goal keeps its savings term as of the forecast date.
    The category chart groups the same payments by purpose, including Uncategorised; both charts have the same monthly totals.
    Funding is spread over all eligible dates through its deadline, even when the deadline is beyond the chart.
    Future-start goals are included from the first eligible allocation date on or after their start date.</p>
<p>Monthly payments round up to pennies and are capped at the outstanding projected remainder, so the final payment may be smaller.
    Goals with no feasible allocation date are included in the current month and flagged for immediate attention, even if their start date is in the future.
    This means the forecast can differ from today's Required monthly savings.</p>
<p>This is a read-only plan assuming those payments are made, not a payment instruction or an account transfer.
    It does not predict interest, inflation, income, or new goals. Refresh after changes; date-sensitive pages also check for local date changes every 30 seconds.</p>
<h2>Holiday calendar status</h2>
<button class="btn btn-outline-secondary mb-3" disabled="@Busy" @onclick="LoadAsync">Refresh calendar status</button>
@if (Error is not null)
{
    <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">@Error</div>
    @if (_holidays is not null)
    {
        <p role="status">Displayed calendar status is from the last successful refresh.</p>
    }
}
@if (_holidays is not null)
{
    <p id="holiday-calendar-source">
        Holiday data source: @_holidays.Source.
        Coverage through: @(_holidays.CoveredThrough?.ToString("dd MMM yyyy") ?? "Unavailable").
        Last successful refresh: @(_holidays.LastSuccessfulRefreshUtc?.ToUniversalTime().ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm 'UTC'") ?? "Unavailable").
    </p>
    @if (_holidays.Warning is not null || _holidays.IsStale)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">@(_holidays.Warning ?? "Holiday data may be out of date.")</div>
    }
}
else
{
    <p>@(Busy ? "Loading calendar status..." : "Calendar status has not loaded. Retry with Refresh calendar status.")</p>
}

@code {
    private HolidayCalendarResponse? _holidays;
    protected override Task OnInitializedAsync() => LoadAsync();
    private async Task LoadAsync() => await PerformAsync(async () => _holidays = (await Api.GetDashboardAsync()).HolidayCalendar);
}
